        "example": {
          "problem": "Light travels from air (n₁ = 1) into water (n₂ = 1.33) at an angle of incidence 60°. Find the angle of refraction.",
          "solution": "Using Snell's Law: 1 × sin(60°) = 1.33 × sin(r). So sin(r) = sin(60°) / 1.33 = 0.866 / 1.33 ≈ 0.651. Therefore r ≈ 40.6°. Light bends toward the normal when entering a denser medium."
        },
        "inSimpleWords": "Light bends when moving between air and water—that's why objects in water look shallower and shifted than they actually are.",
        "emoji": "💧"
