          "solution": "Amol says: 'Because I will know. Every time I eat a cherry, every time I see Sharma Uncle, I'll remember. And I won't be able to look myself in the mirror. Dadi says that silence doesn't erase what happened—it just makes us carry it alone. Confession is heavy, but hiding is heavier.'"
